SDD-TEXT 0.2
Diagram DG-001 "AEB Help Center: Information Architecture"
  description="Public German content hierarchy observed on 2026-10-05: all 8 categories and 73 sections, one representative real article and the public community topic, plus home-level utility and external navigation. The article and post collections are not enumerated. Parallel browse edges, breadcrumb navigation and the secondary community post-creation destination are retained in the SDD but omitted from this overview. CONTAINS is content parentage; NAVIGATES_TO is document navigation."
  diagram_type="ia_place_map"
  scope="Anonymous public site. Authenticated content is not inventoried."
  evidence="Public Zendesk category and section APIs, community topic API, rendered pages and browser interaction checks."
  inventory_sources="https://service.aeb.com/api/v2/help_center/de/categories.json?per_page=100 ; https://service.aeb.com/api/v2/help_center/de/sections.json?per_page=100 ; https://service.aeb.com/api/v2/community/topics.json?per_page=100"
END

Diagram DG-002 "AEB Help Center: UI Contracts"
  description="Composition of ten inspected concrete pages: home, Trade Compliance category, glossary category, Compliance Screening parent section, its article-list section, Customs release-planning section, one real article, search, community home and news topic. Shared components are actual front-end structures, not template Places. Local state-mode changes show section filtering and the newsletter overlay. Repeated filter changes within the already-filtered mode remain in the SDD and component contract but their self-loop is omitted from this overview. Page-to-page navigation belongs to the IA model."
  diagram_type="ui_contracts"
  scope="Representative UI coverage, not an exhaustive UI inventory of every section or article. Component inputs and outputs describe visible browser contracts, not unpublished application APIs."
  limitations="Support-request form blocked by Cloudflare. No sign-in, votes, comments, posts, newsletter subscription or support request was submitted."
END

